From: Philip DiSarro <philipdisarro@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:28:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Value: blaster-friendly denotation restatement + algebra
 lemmas

Restate every Value denotation walk as an explicit first-order pattern-match
recursion (no List.all/any/find?/foldl-with-lambda, no projection lambdas):
Blaster's SMT translation cannot digest the stdlib combinators (3 of 4
containment lemmas Undetermined, one hard translate error), while hand-rolled
recursions close in seconds. Public names, signatures and semantics are
unchanged; *_eq_* lemmas in Basic.lean prove each restatement equal to the
original stdlib-combinator formulation, and all unit tests, the decode gate
and the CEK dispatch tests still pass.

New PlutusCore/Value/Algebra.lean: the four builtin-algebra lemma groups
(plain Lean proofs, sorry-free, reusable via have-feeding):
- lookupCoin_insertCoin_hit/_miss (incl. the amt=0 delete arm)
- lookupCoin_unionValue + unionValue_none (overflow side) + unionValue_sorted
- valueContains_iff + valueContains_none_iff (both negative-error arms)
- unValueData_normalized / valueData_unValueData / unValueData_valueData /
  unValueData_lookup (+ lookupData first-order Data walk), with
  valueSorted/valueNormalized well-formedness predicates and
  valueNormalized_sorted bridging decode results into the other groups.

Blaster smoke on the restated forms: induction <;> blaster closes the
previously-Undetermined lemma shapes in ~2s.
